            "className": "PersistentOfflineOrderStats",
            "doc": "An array that grows: append(v) appends, and queries on any a[l..r] can come in between. Every value that will ever be added is given up front (only to compress them: nothing is added until you push it), so the persistent seg tree is over compressed ranks and costs are log N, never log U: version p holds a[0..p-1], a[l..r] is version r + 1 minus version l, and each append adds one version. Query arguments (x, lowVal, ...) can be anything. 0-indexed. rangeMex: a second persistent tree, over the values 0..(# of distinct values) + 1, holding each value's last index. T: int, long long, ....",
