            "className": "ClampMinTree",
            "doc": "Range add / assign / chmin / chmax with range min queries, plus point ops. All indices 0-based, ranges inclusive [l, r]. Iterative 2N lazy tree: values on the leaves, a tag on each internal node meaning \"applied here, not yet pushed to my children\". The tag is the map x -> min(hi, max(lo, x + add)); these maps compose into the same form, and each is monotone, so it sends a node's min / max straight to the new min / max. Assign v is the clamp with hi = lo = v. An update pushes the tags on its two boundary paths, tags the covering nodes, then rebuilds the two paths.",
