            "doc": "An array whose ranges you can sort in place (ascending or descending), amortized O(log N + log U) a sort, with point reads / writes, rangeAssign, range sums, range maxes, range ors, range ands and the whole array. It is kept as a sequence of sorted runs: each run is a dynamic value seg tree over [valLo, valHi] (copies per node) and an up / down flag, and a Fenwick tree over positions marks where runs start, and a seg tree over positions holds each run's sum / max / or / and at its start. Sorting [l, r] cuts the runs at l and r + 1 and merges every run inside into one; a[i] is the k-th value of the run holding it; a query cuts at l and r + 1 too, then reads whole runs. Merges cost about as many nodes as they free and every run is merged away at most once, hence the amortized bounds. Indices 0-based, ranges inclusive, every index is a position in the current array.",
