            "doc": "Segment tree beats: range chmax (a[i] = max(a[i], x)) and range assign, with range sums and the range max / min, plus point ops. All indices 0-based, ranges inclusive. How it works: a chmax only changes the min values of a node it covers, so a node keeps its min, its strict second min and how many copies of the min it has; a chmax x with mn < x < mn2 moves just those copies (the sum rises by (x - mn) * cntMn) and stops there, and only x >= mn2 has to go further down. A node's own mn doubles as its pending clamp: push clamps each child to it, so there is no chmin / chmax tag. There is no assign tag either: when all of a node's values are equal (no second min), push hands that value to both children as an assign. Amortized O(log N) per update (beats: every extra descent removes a distinct value).",
