            "doc": "Implicit treap: an array you can insert into / erase from anywhere, rotate, move ranges, and cut out into a treap of its own / paste a treap into, each in O(logN) expected, plus point ops, rangeMin, rangeMax, range hashes / isPalindrome / rangesEqual (polynomial hashes mod 2^61 - 1 both ways, the base random per run; a reverse swaps them). All indices 0-based, ranges inclusive [l, r], and an index always means the position in the CURRENT array. Nodes keep their values in array order (an in-order walk); a node's position is the size of everything left of it. Lazy tags mean \"already applied to this node, not yet to its children\". T: int, long long, ...; values are stored as T.",
